//! The sound library's four-slot sequence player, the gameplay player's
//! pose/state/effect queries, and the character-select lifecycle.
//!
//! # What this module covers
//!
//! Eight hundred and eighty-one functions (830 ledgered plus 51 untabled
//! bodies) from three evidence lanes, grouped by the
//! different things this game calls a "player":
//!
//! * the **sequence player** (sound) - a fixed table of four `0xA8`-byte
//!   **player slots** in BSS, the pool pair that stages their buffers, the two
//!   `OSAlarm` timers each slot carries, and the asynchronous-completion
//!   handlers that advance the slot state machine. Promoted from the
//!   `r80260_802ed` lane; addresses `0x80270000..0x80270B80`.
//! * the **player actor** (gameplay) - pose, animation and effect queries on
//!   the object the camera follows. Promoted from the `r80040_80080` lane;
//!   addresses `0x80048C40..0x8004CD20`. Wave 3 adds the remaining motion,
//!   animation-rate and effect siblings, `0x8004B290..0x8004D5A0`. Wave 4
//!   continues the speed/landing/effect paths through `0x8004D510` and adds
//!   the shared field accessors at `0x80056C70..0x80057AD0`. Wave 5 adds the
//!   movement-target dispatcher, the alternate animation-rate tables, the
//!   damage predicates, the state-indexed effect/sound tables, and the
//!   position-move helpers at `0x8004A2C0..0x8004F700`. Wave 14 adds the
//!   short attack/power-up poses and the character-swap handlers at
//!   `0x800480D0..0x8004E980`. Wave 22 adds the nine-state motion machine,
//!   the damage gates, hit acceptance, and the five model-effect records at
//!   `0x80048C70..0x80053700`; start at [`fn_80048c70`] or read the table in
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE22_PLAYER.md`. Wave 39 adds the five model-effect-record
//!   binders, the record-mode writers, the `+0x10D4` history shift register, the
//!   `0x8005E4xx` movement-bit stubs and the slot-array leaves at
//!   `0x800534B0..0x8005D090`; start at [`fn_800534b0`] or read the table in
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE39_PLAYER.md`. Wave 49 adds the `+0x1088` scratch-word
//!   rotate, the event-flag predicate and the four `+0xDEC` interface dispatch
//!   wrappers at `0x80057C80..0x80058110`, the two counter bytes at
//!   `0x800581A0..0x80058260`, the `+0x3B0` bit/slot writer at `0x80056370`,
//!   the two sub-object comparators at `0x800565A0..0x800565E0`, the
//!   `0x8005DC..` 12-byte track-entry table initialisers, and the remaining
//!   `+0x04`/`+0x06`/`+0x12` movement-bit leaves at `0x8005E460..0x8005E610`;
//!   start at [`fn_80057c80`] or read the table in
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE49_PLAYER.md`. Wave 63 adds the four-slot player
//!   manager state machine and its slot-mask byte at `0x8005C930..0x8005D0D0`,
//!   plus the `0x8005E6E0..0x8005E9A0` attribute leaves and the spawn wrapper;
//!   start at [`fn_8005c930`] or read
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE63_PLAYER.md`. Wave 72 adds the eight-byte attachment
//!   table at `+0x442` and its mask driver, the `0x800414A0..0x800448A0`
//!   release wrappers, the recursive `+0x30` chain walkers, the `+0x348`
//!   facing/angle leaves and the attach/hold state at
//!   `0x800414A0..0x80047D60`; start at [`fn_800440c0`] or read
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE72_PLAYER.md`. Wave 74 adds the carry/throw manager at
//!   `0x8005B0F0..0x8005C210`, its six-phase state machine and the four-slot
//!   reservation array; start at [`fn_8005b3a0`] or read
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE74_PLAYER.md`. Wave 87 adds the fourteen constant table
//!   getters at `0x80040600..0x80042B30`, the `+0x30` chain-walk and name-compare
//!   twins at `0x800435D0..0x800436B0`, the four conditional teardown wrappers
//!   `0x80044E50..0x80046410`, the `0x80045EF0` sub-object tick, and the
//!   flag/state gates plus `+0x1464` interface leaves at
//!   `0x80046A50..0x8004A790`; start at [`fn_800435d0`] or read
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE87_PLAYER.md`. Wave 88 adds the four-slot spawn-slot
//!   manager: the `+0x12` move-mask writers and the two `0x400`/`0x200` bit
//!   tests at `0x8005E2B0..0x8005E690`, the `0x80354E10`/`0x80354E20` id
//!   tables with their two resolvers, the reset pair, and the per-index
//!   byte/word accessors at `0x8005EA60..0x8005FC70`; start at
//!   [`fn_8005ea60`] or read `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE88_PLAYER.md`. Wave 91 adds the
//!   `+0x13F4..+0x1408` ride-momentum accumulator at
//!   `0x80053940..0x80053E60`, the spawn-slot counter family at
//!   `0x8005FD20..0x8005FFB0`, the event-flag/timer leaves at
//!   `0x800564F0..0x80057860`, and the record initialisers and release wrappers
//!   at `0x8005DC20..0x8005E030`; start at [`fn_80053aa0`] (the accumulator
//!   reset) or read `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE91_PLAYER.md`. Wave 92 adds the
//!   `daFireBall` state-descriptor installer at `0x800414E0`, its four hit and
//!   animation helpers at `0x80040DE0..0x80040F70`, the dokan/lift-ice
//!   sub-object builders at `0x80042480..0x80045710`, the `+0x30` chain leaves
//!   at `0x80044FF0..0x80045D00`, and the actor constructor/destructor pair
//!   with the mode-2 reset hook at `0x800460D0..0x80046FC0`; start at
//!   [`fn_800414e0`] or read `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE92_PLAYER.md`. Wave 97 closes
//!   the bucket: the thirty-five remaining shared-handler getters of the
//!   `0x80044940` / `0x80047270..0x80047380` / `0x8004D6F0..0x8004D810` runs,
//!   the `0x80045A10` fireball/track builder, and the two effect drivers at
//!   `0x800410F0` and `0x80047F10`; start at [`fn_80045a10`] or read
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE97_PLAYER.md`. Wave 98 adds the `0x800556F0` terrain
//!   probe, the `0x80055810..0x80055EF0` edge/ceiling band helpers, the firework
//!   volley and its four-state celebration driver at
//!   `0x8005C2B0..0x8005C6D0`, the frame-record compiler at
//!   `0x8005D100..0x8005DDC0`, the two `0x8005E6xx` thunks, and the
//!   spawn-slot reserve/release pair at `0x8005ED90..0x8005FE30`; start at
//!   [`fn_80055ae0`] or read `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE98_PLAYER.md`. Wave 103 adds the
//!   per-frame motion integrator at `0x80054F80..0x800573F0` (vertical-velocity
//!   selection, the ground/water classifier, the target-slope latch and the two
//!   rotated-offset builders), the effect-slot inserters `0x80058B20` /
//!   `0x80058EE0`, and the remaining HUD/spawn bookkeeping leaves at
//!   `0x8005BFD0..0x8005F5C0`; start at [`fn_80055330`] or read
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE103_PLAYER.md`. Wave 106 closes the `0x80040000`
//!   bucket: the eight `0x802DCBFC` pointer-to-member forwarders
//!   `0x800408F0..0x8004DB00`, the `+0x3E0` presence-mask driver
//!   [`fn_800441e0`], the nine-record attachment-ring builder
//!   [`fn_80044550`], and the ground-speed damper [`fn_80048630`]; start at
//!   [`fn_800441e0`] or read `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE106_PLAYER.md`. Wave 109 closes
//!   the `0x80050000` bucket: the per-frame input-mask interpreter
//!   [`fn_800544f0`], the two anchor/steering helpers
//!   [`fn_800569c0`]/[`fn_800583a0`], the 37-entry `daPlBase_c` state table
//!   [`fn_800592c0`], and the two spawn-placement passes
//!   [`fn_8005b8a0`]/[`fn_8005ef50`]; start at [`fn_800544f0`] or read
//!   `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE109_PLAYER.md`.
//! * the **character-change select lifecycle** (REL `d_basesNP`) - the last
//!   untranslated teardown, preview-application and animation calls around the
//!   character-select screen. Addresses `0x80601BE0..0x80602FF0` on the
//!   canonical synthetic base `0x80600000`.
//!
//! The three clusters share no data. They meet here only because each is "the
//! player" of its own subsystem. The two leaf byte helpers used when reading
//! actor fields (`0x800483F0`, `0x8004DE30`) live in
//! [`crate::runtime::cpp`].
//!
