/// - Ghidra: `FUN_800577D0` at `0x800577D0` (64 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/800577d0_FUN_800577d0.c`
///
/// Ghidra prints `(double param_1, int param_2)` because it models the float
/// argument as a double and shifts the integer parameter to `r4`. The
/// instruction stream is `fmr f31,f1` with the object in `r3`, so the real
/// signature is `(player, z)`; this translation uses that order.
///
