/// Invokes the pointer-to-member function embedded at `owner + 0x18` with
/// `object` as the receiver and `object`/`owner` as its two arguments.
///
/// The original sets `r5 = owner`, `r3 = r4 = object`, `r12 = owner + 0x18`
/// and tail-calls the member-pointer thunk `0x802DCBFC`; see
/// [`invoke_pmf_d`].
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80063F20` at `0x80063F20` (48 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80063f20_FUN_80063f20.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `owner`: object holding the 12-byte member-pointer record at `+0x18`.
/// - `object`: receiver, passed in `r3` and `r4`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing; the thunk tail-calls the target and the result is discarded.
///
/// # Side effects
/// One indirect call whose arguments are `(object, object, owner)`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `owner + 0x18` must hold a live member-pointer record and the selected
/// method must accept `(this, u32, u32)`.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the three register moves, the `addi r12` and the `bl 0x802DCBFC`
/// are literal, and the body is byte-identical to the wave-210 twin
/// `0x80062090` with only the `addi` displacement changed. Prologue 16 bytes,
/// `blr` at `0x80063F4C` (real body 44 bytes; the `functions.tsv` 48 includes
/// the 4-byte alignment pad that fills `0x80063F4C..0x80063F50`).
pub unsafe fn fn_80063f20(owner: usize, object: usize) {
    invoke_pmf_d(owner + 0x18, object, object as u32, owner as u32);
}

