/// The `addic.` chain at `0x80067298` is the compiler's null test on the
/// adjusted pointer, so the three tests are
/// `this + 0x394 != 0`, `(this + 0x3D4) != 0` and `(this + 0x3EC) != 0`; the
/// same shape repeats for the second member at `+0x3B0`. The two member calls
/// are `0x8015F9F0(member, 0)`, the family release helper with a zero flag.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80067270` at `0x80067270` (168 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80067270_FUN_80067270.c`
/// - Prologue 32 bytes at `0x80067270`, `blr` at `0x80067314`; real extent
///   0xA8 = 168 bytes, matching `functions.tsv`.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: actor object, or `0` (the whole body is skipped).
/// - `delete_flag`: signed; the heap free runs only when it is `> 0`
///   (`cmpi cr0,r30,0` + `bc 4,1`).
