/// `this` unchanged, including the null case (`mr r3,r29` before the epilogue).
///
/// # Side effects
/// Releases the two members at `+0x3EC` and `+0x3B0` through `0x8015F9F0`,
/// destroys the base model with `0x800642B0(this, 0)`, and calls
/// `0x80162920(this)` when `delete_flag > 0`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` must be a live object of this class, or `0`; both members must be
/// valid helper objects when their adjusted pointers are non-null.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the null gates, the two member offsets (`+0x3EC`, `+0x3B0`), the base
/// destructor and the `0 < delete_flag` test are literal. The `-0x394`/`-0x3D4`
/// values Ghidra prints are just the negative forms of the adjusted-pointer
/// tests.
