/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_8006c5c0` at `0x8006C5C0` (64 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/8006c5c0_FUN_8006c5c0.c`
/// - Prologue 20 bytes at `0x8006C5C0` (`stwu`/`mfspr`/`stw`/`stw`/`mr`),
///   `blr` at `0x8006C5FC`; real extent `0x3C` = 60 bytes. The tsv's 64 is the
///   aligned slot up to the next entry at `0x8006C600`.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: live instance; `+0x60` holds the class vtable.
///
/// # Returns
/// `0x801620E0(this)`: `1` when `+0xB` is zero and bit 1 of `+0xF` is clear,
/// `0` otherwise. The epilogue restores only `r1`/`r31`, so the predicate's
/// `r3` is the function's own result - the sub-override `0x8006C8F0` consumes
/// it (`0x8006C8FC: bl 0x8006C5C0`, then `0x8006C900: cmpi cr0,3,r3,0`).
///
