/// Returns `1` when `0x8006C540()` is non-zero, `0` otherwise.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_8006c870` at `0x8006C870` (44 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/8006c870_FUN_8006c870.c`
/// - Prologue 12 bytes at `0x8006C870`, `blr` at `0x8006C898`; real extent
///   `0x2C` = 44 bytes, matching the tsv. The word at `0x8006C880` decodes as
///   `neg r0,r3` (`0x7C0300D0`, XO 104), which is why the raw disassembler
///   prints an unnamed `X31_104` mnemonic.
///
/// # Arguments
/// None.
