// body anywhere in `src`: **39, 42, 44, 48, 49, 50, 51, 52, 53, 54, 55, 56**.
// Slots 35, 40, 41 are `functions.tsv` rows and slots 36, 37, 38, 43, 45, 46,
// 47 already have real `fn_<addr>` definitions (in `game::worldmap`); a prose
// mention such as the constant reference to `0x80065970` in `game::enemies`
// does not count as coverage.
//
// | slot | table word | vtable offset | target | extent | role |
// |---:|---|---:|---|---:|---|
// | 39 | `0x8030856C` | `+0xA4` | `0x80065970` | 144 | copy an owner-query matrix, translate it and keep X/Y |
// | 42 | `0x80308578` | `+0xB0` | `0x80065660` | 84 | spawn `"Wm_en_burst_s"` above the object's position |
// | 44 | `0x80308580` | `+0xB8` | `0x8001D1D0` | 4 | empty virtual hook |
// | 48 | `0x80308590` | `+0xC8` | `0x80065CC0` | 248 | ground-tier gated effect `0x282` |
// | 49 | `0x80308594` | `+0xCC` | `0x80065DC0` | 244 | effect `0x284` plus one of two sounds |
// | 50 | `0x80308598` | `+0xD0` | `0x80065EC0` | 244 | effect `0x283` plus one of two sounds |
// | 51 | `0x8030859C` | `+0xD4` | `0x80046DF0` | 4 | empty virtual hook |
// | 52 | `0x803085A0` | `+0xD8` | `0x800588F0` | 4 | empty virtual hook |
// | 53 | `0x803085A4` | `+0xDC` | `0x800588E0` | 4 | empty virtual hook |
// | 54 | `0x803085A8` | `+0xE0` | `0x80020BE0` | 8 | constant `0` answer |
// | 55 | `0x803085AC` | `+0xE4` | `0x80056BC0` | 8 | store the argument at `+0x1090` |
// | 56 | `0x803085B0` | `+0xE8` | `0x80056D40` | 8 | constant `2` answer |
//
// The twelve bodies measure **1004 B** prologue-to-`bclr`
// (144, 84, 4, 248, 244, 244, 4, 4, 4, 8, 8, 8). None is a `functions.tsv` row,
// so none has a Ghidra export and none gets a `ledger/agents/` entry. The four
// large bodies appear in the wave-226 prologue-verified corpus with exactly the
// measured sizes (144, 84, 248, 244, 244); the eight 4/8-byte leaves are not in
// it. Extents come from the same recursive-descent walker the wave-232 pass
// used: conditional branches and intra-function `b` targets are followed,
// `bctrl` falls through, and the walk stops at `bclr 20,0`/`bcctr`/`rfi`.
//
// These bodies are **shared**: the same twelve addresses also fill slots of the
// WorldMap vtable `0x80325420` (39/42/44/48/49/50), the `dEn_c` vtable
// `0x80314060` (39/42/44/48) and the `WM_PLAYER_VTABLE` `0x80326794`
// (39/42/44/48/49/50/54/55/56), so the translations in this module describe the
// same code those class vtables dispatch to.
//
// SDA bases are this module's usual `r2 = 0x80433080` and `r13 = 0x8042F680`.
// The three `r13` words (`0x80429EE8`, `0x80429D60`, `0x80429DD0`) are already
// named by the wave-97 constants [`W97_EFFECT_MANAGER_80429EE8`],
// [`W97_EFFECT_OWNER_80429D60`] and [`W97_EFFECT_POS_80429DD0`], and the three
// callees `0x800929F0`, `0x80198C30`, `0x80078410` (`0x8006A4B0` as well) are
// the same ones [`fn_800410f0`] drives. Those constants are reused rather than
// duplicated.

