/// incoming float in `+0xEC` (the vertical/landing speed field), and calls the
/// actor's `+0x294` state slot with the `WaitJump` descriptor
/// [`E246_WAITJUMP_DESCRIPTOR_8035465C`] and mode `0`. The answer is then `1`;
/// both rejected paths answer `0`.
///
/// Unlike the five defaults above it, this body really uses its receiver and
/// its `f1`, so the vtable slot takes `(actor, f32) -> u32`.
///
/// # Original (untabled)
/// - Address: `0x80057B90`, 148 B (`stwu r1,-0x20`; `mfspr r0,LR`; the
///   `f31`/`psq_st`/`r31` save block; the two gates; `stfs` at `+0x10C` and
///   `+0xEC`; `lwz r12,0x60(r3)` + `lwz r12,0x294(r12)` + `bcctr`; `li r3,1`;
///   restore and `bclr` at `0x80057C20`; nothing but zero words up to
///   `0x80057C30`)
/// - Table: slot 255 of `0x803084D0`, i.e. vtable offset `+0x404`; also slot
///   255 of `0x8032679C` and the mixed run entry `0x80325824`
/// - Reach: `vcall(actor, 0x404, f32)`
/// - Not in `functions.tsv`; no Ghidra export
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `player`: gameplay player object; `+0x10C` (speed) and `+0xEC` (vertical
///   speed) are written, `+0x60` is the class vtable.
/// - `speed`: the float stored in `+0xEC` before the state switch.
///
/// # Returns
/// `1` after the state switch, `0` when the actor is damaged or flag `4` is
/// set.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Writes `+0x10C` and `+0xEC`; calls [`fn_8004dd00`], [`fn_80056cf0`] and the
/// actor's `+0x294` virtual, which swaps the state descriptor and its
/// animation.
///
/// # Safety
/// `player + 0x60` must hold a live vtable whose `+0x294` slot accepts
/// `(descriptor, 0)`, and `player + 0xEC` must be writable.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - both gates, both stores, the descriptor address and the
/// `li r3,1` return are literal in the disassembly.
pub unsafe fn fn_80057b90(player: usize, speed: f32) -> u32 {
    if fn_8004dd00(player) != 0 {
        return 0;
    }
    if fn_80056cf0(player, 4) != 0 {
        return 0;
    }

    platform::write_f32(player + 0x10C, 0.0);
    platform::write_f32(player + 0xEC, speed);
    let _ = call_actor_slot3(
        player,
        0x294,
        E246_WAITJUMP_DESCRIPTOR_8035465C as u32,
        0,
    );
    1
}

