// ===========================================================================
// Wave 282 lane D (`_D282`) - the `0x80307910` actor-family base vtable
// ===========================================================================
//
// **Shape.** `0x80307910` is a virtual-method table, not a state table or a
// plain array. It is made of a two-word RTTI header `{0, 0}` at
// `0x80307910`/`0x80307914`, a null slot 0 at `0x80307918` (the base class
// declares the slot but emits no body), and 71 implemented method words
// `0x8030791C..0x80307A34`. That 71-word run is the "array" the wave-282
// census names after `0x80307914`; the whole block spans
// `0x80307910..0x80307A38` (296 bytes).
//
// | item | value |
// |---|---|
// | vtable pointer / header | `0x80307910` = `{0, 0}` |
// | slot 0 | `0x80307918` = `0` (null / pure) |
// | 71 method slots | `0x8030791C..0x80307A34` (284 bytes) |
// | following word | `0x80307A38` = `0x6733642F` = `"g3d/"` |
//
// **Install site.** Only two sites in the image write `0x80307910`: the two
// `d_basesNP` derived constructors, each storing it at `object + 0x60` before
// building the `+0x3DC` member and then overwriting it with the derived class
// table:
//
// ```text
// ; 0x806C9080 - allocate 0x4F0 and construct
// 0x806C90A8: lis  r4,0x8030
// 0x806C90B0: addi r4,r4,0x7910     ; 0x80307910
// 0x806C90B4: stw  r4,r31+0x60      ; base vtable during member construction
// 0x806C90B8: bl   0x8007F7A0       ; build the +0x3DC member
// 0x806C90C8: stw  r4,r31+0x60      ; 0x807F9700, the derived vtable
//
// ; 0x80717AE0 - allocate 0x4A10 and construct
// 0x80717B0C: lis  r4,0x8030
// 0x80717B14: addi r4,r4,0x7910     ; 0x80307910
// 0x80717B18: stw  r4,r31+0x60
// 0x80717B1C: bl   0x8007F7A0
// 0x80717B2C: stw  r3,r31+0x60      ; 0x80807DC0, the derived vtable
// ```
//
// The derived tables keep the same slot grid but override 11 slots each:
// `0, 6, 9, 16, 20, 21, 24, 25, 27, 29, 44` (slot 0 is the base's pure slot;
// slots 20/21/24/25/27/29/44 are the same seven `d_basesNP` thunks in both
// derived tables). The other 61 slots below are shared unchanged.
